<h1>relation</h1>
<p>
(definition)
</p>

<p>
<strong>Definition:</strong>
A computation which takes some inputs and yields an output.  Any particular input may yield different outputs at different times. Formally, a mapping from each element in the <a href="domain.html"><em>domain</em></a> to one or more elements in the <a href="range.html"><em>range</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<strong>Specialization</strong> (... is a kind of me.)<br>
<a href="function.html"><em>function</em></a>, <a href="binaryRelation.html"><em>binary relation</em></a>.
</p>

<p>
<em>Note:
Cosine is a function, since every angle has a specific cosine. Its inverse cos<sup>-1</sup>(x) is a relation, since a cosine value maps to many (for this relation, infinitely many) angles.</em>
</p>

<p>Author: <a href="../Other/contrib.html#authorPEB">PEB</a></p>

